# ===========================================================================
# OS1 Fiber Track Pro - BASE Caddyfile (committed, read-only in the proxy).
#
# This file is deliberately tiny and static. It contains NO per-domain config
# and NO operator-supplied text. All real site blocks (the hostnames operators
# add in Settings -> Domain & SSL, with their reverse_proxy upstreams) are
# GENERATED by the app from structured values only and written to the shared
# caddy_generated volume. This base file simply imports whatever the app has
# generated. Caddy is started with --watch, so a regenerated import file is
# hot-reloaded with no restart.
#
# Security model:
#   * Operators never write raw Caddy directives. The UI/API accept only a
#     validated hostname; the app renders the site block itself (reverse_proxy
#     to the app upstream + encode), then validates the generated file against
#     an allow-list before writing it here for import.
#   * Certificate private keys, the ACME account key and renewal state live in
#     the caddy_data volume only. They are never read by the app, stored in the
#     database, returned by any API, or written to logs.
# ===========================================================================

{
	# Global options. Caddy's automatic HTTPS (ACME via Let's Encrypt) is on by
	# default for every hostname that appears in an imported site block; issuance,
	# OCSP stapling, HTTP->HTTPS redirect and renewal are all handled here.
	# Set an operator contact for ACME/expiry notices via the ACME_EMAIL env var.
	email {$ACME_EMAIL}
}

# Pull in every generated per-domain site block. The glob quietly matches
# nothing until the app has written its first config, so the proxy starts
# cleanly on a fresh install with no domains configured yet.
import /caddy-generated/*.caddy
